## Good morning!

Another day, one more black coffee, I maintained my streak of solving crossword on [the Elevate app](https://elevateapp.com/) and played some other games to improve my reading and comprehension skills.

On the way to the office, listened to this interesting [podcast](https://open.spotify.com/episode/07ZgtAKWnnTWjpgIyr8ggP?si=fa46a7e0efdf405f) - Lose Yourself: The secret to Fiding flow and Being Fully present which basically explained why I turned to the elevate app in the morning rather than reading a book. Answer is I preferred to maintain that streak on that app over reading a book that I didn't start to read yet(also, reading is boring -.-", but its important, I reckon). Here are the key take aways:
* Rather than running behind 'mindfulness', 'being in the present' ideology, start practing the 'flow state' which basically means get into that goldilock zone where you optimize the challenge and reward aspects. 
* Reduction of uncertainity is something which drives us to do anything and gets us into the flow state. So, increase the uncertainity of any task and you will find yourself doing it with more interest. 
* Be a better communicator - off topic but something for me to work on, be more clear, specific and trustworthy.


